{"name":"Jamaica Bay","hex":"#95cbc4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Jamaica Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An estuary on the southern portion of the western tip of Long Island, New York, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Jamaica_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jamaica Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Jamaica Bay is an estuary on the southern portion of the western tip of Long Island, in the U.S. state of New York. The estuary is partially man-made, and partially natural. The bay connects with Lower New York Bay to the west, through Rockaway Inlet, and is the westernmost of the coastal lagoons on the south shore of Long Island. Politically, it is primarily divided between the boroughs of Brooklyn and Queens in New York City, with a small part touching Nassau County."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/JamaicaBay.jpeg/330px-JamaicaBay.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamaica_Bay","wikidata":"Q1679819"},{"title":"Jamaica","blocks":[{"text":"Jamaica is an island country in the Caribbean, covering 10,991 square kilometres (4,244 sq mi). It is the third-largest island in the Greater Antilles and the Caribbean, after Cuba and the island of Hispaniola. Jamaica lies about 145 km (78 nmi) south of Cuba, 191 km (103 nmi) west of Hispaniola, and 215 km (116 nmi) southeast of the Cayman Islands. With 2.8 million people, Jamaica is the third-most populous Anglophone country in the Americas and the fourth-most populous country in the Caribbean. Kingston is the capital and largest city."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Flag_of_Jamaica.svg/330px-Flag_of_Jamaica.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamaica","wikidata":"Q766"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Jamaica_Bay_aerial_from_NW_01_-_white_balanced_%289457234768%29.jpg/500px-Jamaica_Bay_aerial_from_NW_01_-_white_balanced_%289457234768%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Jamaica_Bay_aerial_from_NW_01_-_white_balanced_%289457234768%29.jpg/1280px-Jamaica_Bay_aerial_from_NW_01_-_white_balanced_%289457234768%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Jamaica_Bay_aerial_from_NW_01_-_white_balanced_%28945723476